From 9eb41135c6f032e743e94110c699d8e378b9e6cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:57:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1145/1157] fix(kanban): a remote notice's ledger ack means a
 transcript row [daveey]

A dead holder's claim was acked delivered=1 when the chat's lineage had ANY
"Kanban <task id> " line: notice_in_transcript's legacy text fallback ran for
keyed claims too. Hub card t_b49c4888 blocked again (blocked@1793336479), the
claiming Desktop backend was replaced by the 22:06 PDT core update, and its
successor acked ledger row 1245 against the 16:03 notice of the card's
previous block; the chat never saw the new block (example-laptop 2026-10-29).

- A keyed claim is proven only by its own key; the task-id text match stays
  for unkeyed legacy rows (_reconcile_legacy).
- delivered=1 (DELIVERED) is set only by ack after the transcript write or by
  a keyed transcript hit. Stale / placeholder settles are SETTLED (2) and get
  a swept row with a reason; swept gains a reason column (delivered,
  transcript, stale, placeholder). The dead-holder ack logs a line.

Builds on 5bab4bb450 (in-flight claims); RED on the old code for both the
poller and the sweeper/waker path.
